  "title": "Vegetarian Mexican Tortilla Layered Bake",
  "image": "generated://dishcovery/9000021.jpg",
  "readyInMinutes": 55,
  "servings": 6,
  "summary": "Celebrate authentic southwestern flavors with this comforting Mexican casserole that is <b>entirely vegetarian from top to bottom</b>. Layers of lightly charred corn tortillas, spiced black beans, roasted poblano peppers, and tangy salsa verde create a rich stack of savory textures. Fresh cotija cheese and shredded oaxacan cheese melt between every level, forming a creamy interior capped by a golden browned top crust. Seasoned with cumin, coriander, and fresh oregano, the bean filling offers satisfying substance that easily pleases vegetarians and meat-eaters alike. Baking the casserole slowly allows the tart green salsa to soak into the hearty tortilla layers while mellowing the heat of the roasted peppers. Serve warm with sliced avocado and freshly chopped cilantro for a crowd-pleasing dinner that highlights wholesome plant-based ingredients. Perfect for meal prep, leftovers reheat beautifully without losing their structural integrity.",
